\subsection{Random Effect Specification Tests}

Likelihood Ratio Test results for models with and without a third level of 
year effects. In all cases the year effects should be retained. I used the 
simulated finite sample distribution of the Restricted Likelihood Ratio Test 
\citep{rlrt1, rlrt2, rlrt3}. Computation implemented using the \texttt{RLRsim} 
package for R \citep{rlrt2}. 


<<LRTresults, echo=FALSE, results='hide'>>=
# Lag Model LRT
print(lagLRT)
# Competitive Model LRT
print(closeLRT)
# Party Model LRT
print(partyLRT)
# Teacher Model LRT
print(teachLRT)

lagLRT$p.value <- ifelse(lagLRT$p.value < 0.01, 0.01, lagLRT$p.value)
closeLRT$p.value <- ifelse(closeLRT$p.value < 0.01, 0.01, closeLRT$p.value)
partyLRT$p.value <- ifelse(partyLRT$p.value < 0.01, 0.01, partyLRT$p.value)
teachLRT$p.value <- ifelse(teachLRT$p.value < 0.01, 0.01, teachLRT$p.value)
@


\begin{myitemize}
\item Lag Model: p-value < \Sexpr{lagLRT$p.value}
\item Competitiveness Model: p-value < \Sexpr{closeLRT$p.value}
\item Partisanship Model: p-value < \Sexpr{partyLRT$p.value}
\item Teacher Influence Model: p-value < \Sexpr{teachLRT$p.value}
\end{myitemize}

\subsection{Additional Substantive Effect Plots}

Figure \ref{fig:randomEffectplot2} shows the standardized intercepts for each 
election cycle -- here the year effects are measured in standard deviations from 
the grand average of 0 marked by the red line. From 2004 to 2009 elections were 
relatively consistent with one another in terms of turnout. From 2010 to 2012, 
turnout was first depressed, and then heightened across the state. Most interestingly 
is that two years of elevated turnout across the state (net of district-election and 
district-average effects) were in 2011 and 2012 after the election of Governor Scott Walker and the introduction of Act 10. 

<<rePlotHide2, fig.show='hide'>>=
replotdf <- 1
while(class(replotdf) != "data.frame"){
  replotdf <- try(substEffSimRE(mixedModclose, "year", ncases = 1, alpha = 0.1), 
                  silent = TRUE)
}

replotdf$year <- as.character(replotdf$year)

replotdf$yhatUnscale <- (replotdf[, "yhat"] * 2 * moddatScaleParty[1, 2]) + moddatScaleParty[1, 1]
replotdf$yhatUnscale <- replotdf$yhatUnscale / 100
replotdf$lwrUnscale <- (replotdf[, "lwr"] * 2 * moddatScaleParty[1, 2]) + moddatScaleParty[1, 1]
replotdf$lwrUnscale <- replotdf$lwrUnscale / 100
replotdf$uprUnscale <- (replotdf[, "upr"] * 2 * moddatScaleParty[1, 2]) + moddatScaleParty[1, 1]
replotdf$uprUnscale <- replotdf$uprUnscale / 100

lowerBar <- ((quantile(fitted(mixedModP), prob = 0.2) * 2 * moddatScaleParty["turnout", 2]) + 
      moddatScaleParty["turnout", 1]) /100
upperBar <- ((quantile(fitted(mixedModP), prob = 0.8) * 2 * moddatScaleParty["turnout", 2]) + 
      moddatScaleParty["turnout", 1]) / 100

ggplot(data = replotdf, aes(x = year, y = yhatUnscale, 
                            ymin = lwrUnscale, ymax = uprUnscale)) + 
  geom_errorbar(width = .4) + geom_point()+
  theme_dpi(base_size=12) + 
  theme(
                      strip.text = element_blank(), 
                      strip.background = element_blank(), 
                      panel.grid.minor = element_blank()) + 
  geom_hline(yintercept = lowerBar, linetype = 2) + 
  geom_hline(yintercept = upperBar, linetype = 2) + 
  facet_wrap(~caseID, ncol = 1) + 
  labs(x = "Year", y = "Predicted SB Turnout") + 
  scale_y_continuous(label = percent)


plotdf <- REsim(mixedModP, nsims = 1000)
plotdf <- plotdf[plotdf$level == "Level 2",]
p1 <- plotMCMCre(plotdf, scale = 1.96, var = "mean", 
               sd = "sd", sigmaScale = sigma(mixedModP)) + 
  labs(title = "Partisan Model", x= "District", y = "Intercept")+ 
  ylim(c(-2, 3.5))
plotdf <- REsim(mixedModclose, nsims = 1000)
plotdf <- plotdf[plotdf$level == "Level 2",]
p2 <- plotMCMCre(plotdf, scale = 1.96, var = "mean", 
                 sd = "sd", sigmaScale = sigma(mixedModclose)) + 
  labs(title = "Competitiveness Model", x= "District", y = "Intercept")+ 
  ylim(c(-2, 3.5))
plotdf <- REsim(mixedModteach, nsims = 1000)
plotdf <- plotdf[plotdf$level == "Level 2",]
p3 <- plotMCMCre(plotdf, scale = 1.96, var = "mean", 
                 sd = "sd", sigmaScale = sigma(mixedModteach))+ 
  labs(title = "Teach Share Model", x= "District", y = "Intercept")+ 
  ylim(c(-2, 3.5))
plotdf <- REsim(mixedMod1lagsb, nsims = 1000)
plotdf <- plotdf[plotdf$level == "Level 2",]

grid.arrange(p1, p2, p3, main = "Variance in Year Intercepts Across Models")
@

<<randomEffectplot2, eval=TRUE, fig.scap="Comparing Year Effects for Turnout",fig.height=4, fig.cap="Estimated year effects in model effect size terms. Each point represents the estimated standard deviation increase or decrease in turnout for a given election year across all school districts. Confidence intervals are the 90 percent confidence interval across 1000 simulations of the model random effects.">>=

plotdf$median <- plotdf$median / sigma(mixedMod1lagsb)
plotdf$sd <- plotdf$sd / sigma(mixedMod1lagsb)

ggplot(plotdf, aes(x = as.numeric(X1), y = median, ymin = median - 1.6 * sd, 
       ymax = median + 1.6*sd)) + geom_pointrange() + 
  labs(x= "Year", y = "Intercept", "Year Effect Sizes") + 
  scale_x_continuous(breaks = c(2003:2012), labels = c(2003:2012)) + 
  scale_y_continuous(breaks = seq(-1.5, 1.5, by = .25)) + 
  geom_hline(yintercept = 0, size =I(1.05), color = I("red")) +
  theme(axis.text.x=element_text(), panel.grid = element_line(), 
         panel.grid.major = element_line(linetype="dotted", colour ="black"),
        panel.grid.major.x = element_blank(), 
         panel.grid.minor = element_blank(), 
         panel.background = element_rect(fill = "white", colour = NA), 
            panel.border = element_rect(fill = NA, colour = "grey50"), 
        axis.title = element_text(size = rel(0.8), face = "bold"), 
            axis.title.y = element_text(vjust = 0.35, angle = 90), 
            axis.text = element_text(size = rel(0.8), colour = "black"), 
        axis.ticks = element_line(colour = "black", 
                size = rel(1.5)), legend.key = element_rect(colour = "grey80"), 
            legend.title = element_text(), legend.text = element_text())
@


